/T (To get started with research, begin by choosing a topic that genuinely interests you and reading a few recent, relevant papers to understand the current state of the field. Look for unanswered questions or areas that can be improved, and then formulate a focused, testable research question. Starting small - by reproducing an existing study and making incremental improvements - is often the most practical and effective way to build confidence and develop strong research skills.  )
