<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E ("Working on a project on molecular docking chemistry - a term I hadn't heard until my supervisor mentioned it - was eye-opening, and a series of learning and relearning the basic concepts of chemistry," Zainab says. The project reshaped how she thinks about coagulation and pushed her to go deeper into water chemistry and water treatment more broadly. Presenting to her supervisor and other researchers, and fielding their questions, proved just as valuable as the computation itself - pointing the work in a better direction and surfacing angles that might otherwise have been missed.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (Access to clean water remains one of the most persistent infrastructure gaps across the continent, and the coagulants used to treat it are too often chosen by trial and error rather than by design.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
