295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 122 0 R
/T (Career breaks for parenthood and caregiving are common - but their long-term effect on a STEM academic's career trajectory is rarely studied with any rigor. At Aalto University, Ukachi worked as a research assistant on a project examining exactly that: how career breaks due to parenthood and caregiving shape the careers of STEM academics, and what kind of network support helps people navigate those breaks without losing momentum in their field.)
/E (Career breaks for parenthood and caregiving are common - but their long-term effect on a STEM academic's career trajectory is rarely studied with any rigor. At Aalto University, Ukachi worked as a research assistant on a project examining exactly that: how career breaks due to parenthood and caregiving shape the careers of STEM academics, and what kind of network support helps people navigate those breaks without losing momentum in their field.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 122 0 R
/T (It's a notably different kind of research from the technical, systems-building work featured elsewhere in this issue - qualitative, human-centered, and concerned with the structural realities that shape who stays in STEM and who doesn't. That range is itself worth noting: research skill isn't confined to one methodology, and understanding people's career trajectories takes the same rigor as fine-tuning a model or optimizing a microgrid.)
/E (It's a notably different kind of research from the technical, systems-building work featured elsewhere in this issue - qualitative, human-centered, and concerned with the structural realities that shape who stays in STEM and who doesn't. That range is itself worth noting: research skill isn't confined to one methodology, and understanding people's career trajectories takes the same rigor as fine-tuning a model or optimizing a microgrid.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
