357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 125 0 R
/T (Search-and-rescue robotics doesn't leave much room for theory alone - the environments are rough, unpredictable, and often hazardous by design. Rhoda spent a week at ETH Zurich's RobotX summer school getting exactly that kind of hands-on exposure: lectures and tutorials on core robotics concepts, paired with programming autonomous ground robots built for rough terrain and testing them across varied environments.)
/E (Search-and-rescue robotics doesn't leave much room for theory alone - the environments are rough, unpredictable, and often hazardous by design. Rhoda spent a week at ETH Zurich's RobotX summer school getting exactly that kind of hands-on exposure: lectures and tutorials on core robotics concepts, paired with programming autonomous ground robots built for rough terrain and testing them across varied environments.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 125 0 R
/T (The week ran alongside ARCHE \(Advanced Robotic Capabilities for Hazardous Environments\), which brought legged robots, teleoperated excavators, amphibious vehicles, and UAVs into simulated disaster scenarios - giving participants a front-row view of how different robotic platforms are designed to complement each other when a single robot type isn't enough for the job.)
/E (The week ran alongside ARCHE \(Advanced Robotic Capabilities for Hazardous Environments\), which brought legged robots, teleoperated excavators, amphibious vehicles, and UAVs into simulated disaster scenarios - giving participants a front-row view of how different robotic platforms are designed to complement each other when a single robot type isn't enough for the job.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 125 0 R
/T ("A highlight was meeting professors and hearing the guest lectures, along with getting to see many different kinds of robots in action," Rhoda says. "It was also very hands on.")
/E ("A highlight was meeting professors and hearing the guest lectures, along with getting to see many different kinds of robots in action," Rhoda says. "It was also very hands on.")
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
