384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (The fine-tuned edge models cut average word error rate from 64.9% to 38.0% - showing that domain specialization can outweigh raw scale for real-world African speech. The team also found that model architecture tracks language family, and that standard WER understates performance for syllabary scripts like Ge'ez. All 57 fine-tuned models, the cleaned data, and the code are released openly, giving practitioners usable ASR for languages that previously had none.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
