/P 127 0 R
/T (Paper Title: SynapFlow at BioASQ@CLEF 2026  \(Biomedical Retrieval-Augmented Generation\))
/E (Paper Title: SynapFlow at BioASQ@CLEF 2026  \(Biomedical Retrieval-Augmented Generation\))
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 127 0 R
/T (When a clinician queries a biomedical database, the top-ranked results often say the same thing in slightly different ways - a familiar failure mode that starves a downstream language model of the varied evidence it needs to reason well. John's paper, presented at the BioASQ track of CLEF 2026, an international evaluation forum for information access systems, tackles that redundancy head-on.)
/E (When a clinician queries a biomedical database, the top-ranked results often say the same thing in slightly different ways - a familiar failure mode that starves a downstream language model of the varied evidence it needs to reason well. John's paper, presented at the BioASQ track of CLEF 2026, an international evaluation forum for information access systems, tackles that redundancy head-on.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 127 0 R
/T (Working with Prof. Eric Nyberg of CMU's Language Technologies Institute, John built a weighted hybrid retrieval pipeline that introduces Maximal Marginal Relevance as a post-reranking filter - sitting on the output of a neural re-ranker to prune redundant passages before generation. Prior biomedical QA work had used MMR only as a first-pass retrieval strategy; applying it after a neural re-ranker to explicitly enforce diversity in a RAG pipeline is, to their knowledge, a first for the domain. )
/E (Working with Prof. Eric Nyberg of CMU's Language Technologies Institute, John built a weighted hybrid retrieval pipeline that introduces Maximal Marginal Relevance as a post-reranking filter - sitting on the output of a neural re-ranker to prune redundant passages before generation. Prior biomedical QA work had used MMR only as a first-pass retrieval strategy; applying it after a neural re-ranker to explicitly enforce diversity in a RAG pipeline is, to their knowledge, a first for the domain. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 127 0 R
/T (The result is a system that gives the generator a broader, less repetitive evidence base - exactly what a clinician needs when the question at hand doesn't have a single, textbook answer. It's a small architectural change with an outsized effect, and the kind of contribution that quietly moves the field: sharpen a real bottleneck, benchmark it honestly, share the pipeline.)
/E (The result is a system that gives the generator a broader, less repetitive evidence base - exactly what a clinician needs when the question at hand doesn't have a single, textbook answer. It's a small architectural change with an outsized effect, and the kind of contribution that quietly moves the field: sharpen a real bottleneck, benchmark it honestly, share the pipeline.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
