433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 128 0 R
/T (Paper Title: Attention-Guided Structural Pruning for Cross-Modal Alignment Preservation in Vision-Language Models)
/E (Paper Title: Attention-Guided Structural Pruning for Cross-Modal Alignment Preservation in Vision-Language Models)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 128 0 R
/T (Vision-language models learn a delicate alignment between what they see and what they read - the very thing that lets them describe an image or answer a question about it. Making these models smaller is essential for deployment on real hardware, but standard pruning often severs precisely that alignment, quietly degrading the model's cross-modal reasoning even as the accuracy numbers on unimodal benchmarks look fine.)
/E (Vision-language models learn a delicate alignment between what they see and what they read - the very thing that lets them describe an image or answer a question about it. Making these models smaller is essential for deployment on real hardware, but standard pruning often severs precisely that alignment, quietly degrading the model's cross-modal reasoning even as the accuracy numbers on unimodal benchmarks look fine.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
435 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 128 0 R
/T (In their Best-Paper-Award-winning work, Boniface and co-author Jean Gabriel Mpuhwezimana propose using the model's own attention patterns to guide the pruning decision - identifying and preserving the structural components that carry cross-modal information, so what remains after compression is a leaner model whose picture-word alignment is intact. The award recognizes both the clarity of the idea and the care of its execution.)
/E (In their Best-Paper-Award-winning work, Boniface and co-author Jean Gabriel Mpuhwezimana propose using the model's own attention patterns to guide the pruning decision - identifying and preserving the structural components that carry cross-modal information, so what remains after compression is a leaner model whose picture-word alignment is intact. The award recognizes both the clarity of the idea and the care of its execution.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 128 0 R
/T (Making frontier models runnable in the places that most need them - hospitals, classrooms, and phones without a datacenter behind them - is one of the field's quietest but most consequential problems. Compression that respects what a model actually learned is how deployment becomes possible, and how the benefits of these systems reach beyond the labs that trained them.)
/E (Making frontier models runnable in the places that most need them - hospitals, classrooms, and phones without a datacenter behind them - is one of the field's quietest but most consequential problems. Compression that respects what a model actually learned is how deployment becomes possible, and how the benefits of these systems reach beyond the labs that trained them.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
