487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 130 0 R
/T (Paper Title: Optimizing Microgrid Generation & Storage  \(Combinations for Low-Resource Contexts\))
/E (Paper Title: Optimizing Microgrid Generation & Storage  \(Combinations for Low-Resource Contexts\))
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Designing a microgrid for a rural clinic or an off-grid community is a hard sizing problem: how much solar, how much wind, how much battery storage, at what cost, meeting what demand curve - and where every wrong answer is either wasted capital or lights that go out. Kevin's paper, as main author with Prof. Jesse Thornburg, takes on that combinatorial question directly, framing it as an optimization over generation and storage combinations tuned to the constraints of low-resource contexts.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Every one of the hundreds of millions of people still without reliable electricity in Sub-Saharan Africa lives downstream of decisions like the ones this paper is trying to make well. Sound optimization is not a footnote here; it is the difference between a system that lasts and a system that becomes an expensive lesson. Work that treats the constraints of low-resource contexts as first-class design inputs - rather than afterthoughts on a template imported from somewhere else - is exactly the kind of research the region needs more of.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
