/Title (Research is a systematic and purposeful process of investigating a clearly defined question in order to generate new knowledge or deeper understanding. It goes beyond simply gathering information; it requires critical thinking, careful planning, and the use of appropriate methods to test ideas or hypotheses in a structured and reproducible way. In fields such as Engineering, research often involves identifying a gap or limitation in existing work, proposing a meaningful improvement or new approach, and evaluating it through well-designed experiments and thoughtful analysis.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1451 0 R
/Next 1542 0 R
>>
endobj
1542 0 obj
<<
/Title (To get started with research, begin by choosing a topic that genuinely interests you and reading a few recent, relevant papers to understand the current state of the field. Look for unanswered questions or areas that can be improved, and then formulate a focused, testable research question. Starting small - by reproducing an existing study and making incremental improvements - is often the most practical and effective way to build confidence and develop strong research skills.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1451 0 R
/Prev 1541 0 R
>>
