/Title (Africa's second-life battery economy - reusing spent electric-vehicle battery packs to power microgrids - is one of the more promising paths toward affordable off-grid electricity. But the international standards governing this space overwhelmingly regulate end-product performance, not the technicians who dismantle the packs to begin with. Kayesu's paper closes that gap.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1706 0 R
/Next 1742 0 R
>>
