<<
/Title (Vision-language models learn a delicate alignment between what they see and what they read - the very thing that lets them describe an image or answer a question about it. Making these models smaller is essential for deployment on real hardware, but standard pruning often severs precisely that alignment, quietly degrading the model's cross-modal reasoning even as the accuracy numbers on unimodal benchmarks look fine.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1738 0 R
/Next 1767 0 R
>>
endobj
1767 0 obj
<<
/Title (In their Best-Paper-Award-winning work, Boniface and co-author Jean Gabriel Mpuhwezimana propose using the model's own attention patterns to guide the pruning decision - identifying and preserving the structural components that carry cross-modal information, so what remains after compression is a leaner model whose picture-word alignment is intact. The award recognizes both the clarity of the idea and the care of its execution.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1738 0 R
/Prev 1766 0 R
>>
endobj
1768 0 obj
<<
/Title (Co-Author\(s\))
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
