/Title ("Capacity building is not about holding conferences and workshops," Grace reflects. "It is about what people can use without your presence - the tools, guidance, and resources you leave with them, that they can pick up easily in their day-to-day work long after any event is over." Policies are only as strong as the practitioners who can actually implement them - and most of the world's climate guidance is dense, technical, and scattered across formal decision documents. Work that turns that guidance into something a person can actually use is what makes international climate policy real on the ground rather than theoretical on paper.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
