1801 0 obj
<<
/Title (Article 6.4 of the Paris Agreement establishes the international mechanism for greenhouse gas mitigation and sustainable development - but the guidance governing it is scattered across CMA decisions, Supervisory Body rulings, and technical annexes, written in dense legal language, updated frequently, and hard to search. For governments, project developers, and civil society groups engaging with Article 6.4 for the first time - particularly from developing countries and under-resourced institutions - that fragmentation itself becomes a barrier to participation.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1791 0 R
/Next 1802 0 R
>>
endobj
1802 0 obj
<<
/Title (Grace's work during this internship was building the answer to that problem: the Article 6.4 Navigator, a retrieval-augmented generation \(RAG\) system that lets any stakeholder ask a plain-language questions - and receive an answer grounded entirely in official UNFCCC text, with citations back to the exact source document. Under the hood, the system retrieves relevant passages from the official Article 6.4 corpus, uses a language model to draft a plain-language answer from that retrieved context, and returns the answer alongside direct references - so the tool never speculates or substitutes for the official guidance, it simply makes that guidance reachable. Multilingual support aligned with the UN's official languages was built into the design from the outset, since much of Article 6.4's intended audience works in French, Spanish, and Arabic as often as English. Alongside the Navigator, Grace also co-developed the PACM podcast through to its launch and helped design the Technical Expert Review Course from the ground up.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1791 0 R
/Prev 1801 0 R
>>
endobj
