1833 0 obj
<<
/Title (Career breaks for parenthood and caregiving are common - but their long-term effect on a STEM academic's career trajectory is rarely studied with any rigor. At Aalto University, Ukachi worked as a research assistant on a project examining exactly that: how career breaks due to parenthood and caregiving shape the careers of STEM academics, and what kind of network support helps people navigate those breaks without losing momentum in their field.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1826 0 R
/Next 1834 0 R
>>
endobj
1834 0 obj
<<
/Title (It's a notably different kind of research from the technical, systems-building work featured elsewhere in this issue - qualitative, human-centered, and concerned with the structural realities that shape who stays in STEM and who doesn't. That range is itself worth noting: research skill isn't confined to one methodology, and understanding people's career trajectories takes the same rigor as fine-tuning a model or optimizing a microgrid.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1826 0 R
/Prev 1833 0 R
>>
endobj
1835 0 obj
<<
/Title (Some of the most important documents in the world can't leave the building they live in. At the IMF, Glorry spent his summer working on exactly that constraint: adapting a small open-weight vision-language model - around 3B parameters - to extract structured information from multilingual administrative documents, in a setting where the real corpus was confidential and could never be used for training.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1827 0 R
/Next 1836 0 R
>>
endobj
1836 0 obj
<<
/Title (His workaround was to build a synthetic document generator calibrated on aggregate statistics from the real corpus - reproducing realistic layouts, scan and photo artifacts, stamps, and multi-page structures across nine languages. He then fine-tuned the model using parameter-efficient methods \(QLoRA\) on on-premise GPU hardware, and designed the evaluation around leakage-safe held-out splits, per-field accuracy, and significance testing against a zero-shot baseline. The result: the fine-tuned model reached strong extraction accuracy on document categories where the base model had scored zero. Agentic AI tooling ran throughout his daily engineering workflow, giving his practical grounding in the second half of his research area.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1827 0 R
/Prev 1835 0 R
>>
endobj
1837 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1828 0 R
/Next 1840 0 R
>>
endobj
